Source offer for the bundled GCC runtime
========================================

The Nix release artifact ships GCC 16.2.0's runtime under the GNU GPL v3
with the GCC Runtime Library Exception 3.1:

  lib/libstdc++.so.6   shared, train11 layout
  lib/libgcc_s.so.1    shared, train11 layout
  wiz, grail           static libstdc++/libgcc in the Nix build

The GitHub release.yml path links Lean's static libc++ instead; see NOTICE
and LICENSES/lean4-third-party.

Corresponding Source
--------------------

  GCC 16.2.0: https://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/gcc/gcc-16.2.0/gcc-16.2.0.tar.xz

The exact nixpkgs revision is recorded in flake.lock. The Wiz packaging
scripts (scripts/release-tarball.sh, scripts/scrub-store-paths.py) and the
Wiz source are at https://github.com/wiz-pl/wiz.

This file is the written offer for the runtime source. It ships as
share/wiz/SOURCE-OFFER next to the licence texts.
